    "title": "Crews battle massive 6-alarm fire in Allentown; some residents asked to evacuate - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By 6abc Digital Staff ,\n2 hours ago\nA massive six-alarm fire tore through a commercial building in Allentown on Wednesday night.\nThe blaze broke out around 8:45 p.m. in the 300 block of North Front Street.\nChopper 6 video showed heavy flames engulfing the structure, which sustained significant damage. Portions of the roof and interior floors have collapsed.\nAs of 11 p.m., crews were still working to bring the fire under control.\nWATCH: Chopper 6 was overhead as crews battled a massive fire in Allentown, Pa., on June 24, 2026.\nAuthorities urged residents on the 300 block of North Front Street to evacuate through the rear of their homes. Residents in surrounding areas were advised to shelter in place until further notice\nNo injuries have been reported.\nOfficials said those displaced can seek shelter at Resurrected Life Church at 620 W. Hamilton Street.\nSeveral road closures remain in effect as emergency crews continue to work in the area.\nThousands of PPL customers were without power Wednesday night due to the fire.\nThe cause of the blaze remains under investigation.\n4",
    "summary": "By 6abc Digital Staff , A massive six-alarm fire tore through a commercial building in Allentown on Wednesday night. Chopper 6 video showed heavy flames engulfing the structure, which sustained significant damage. WATCH: Chopper 6 was overhead as crews battled a massive fire in Allentown, Pa., on June 24, 2026. Authorities urged residents on the 300 block of North Front Street to evacuate through the rear of their homes. Several road closures remain in effect as emergency crews continue to work in the area.",
